{"from": "text:mishnah-nedarim-1-3", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mt-05-34-35-oaths", "grade": "B", "note": "Nedarim 1:3 treats a vow associating food with 'the altar, the Sanctuary, or Jerusalem' as binding - the live practice of swearing by Jerusalem and holy things that 5:34-35 addresses; Matthew's teaching renounces such oaths. Redacted c. 200 CE, so it may not describe 30 CE practice exactly. Regraded C to B per the architect's Mishnah ruling (2026-11-15): the Mishnah names the same practice the claim states."}
